steveyo wrote on Wed, 05 Nov 2003 16:45:32 GMT in article 
news:<MO9qb.7624$1N3.5151@twister.nyroc.rr.com>:

> Last year, only caveman, rogue and ranger had winning scores under
> 25,000,000.  That high a score is either quasi-extinctionist (cast CM over
> and over), or uses the strategies of repeated killing the toughest monsters.
> Both become boring after a while to me.   Though extinctionist can be fun
> poly-piling and over-enchanting stuff, I find no enjoyment or challenge in
> stoning and stone-to-fleshing Demogorgon 100(000) times in a row.

Yup, the nethack score system is nearly worthless as a measure of what 
you've accomplished in a game -- but isn't that what a score is supposed to 
measure?

> With all that in mind, here's Steveyo's wishful list of Nethack tournament
> prizes, 

> 1. 1st place High Score Ascension
> 2. 1st place High Score for each class

As you pointed out, the high scores are all quasi-extinctionist.  So there's 
no point in distinguishing by class; every class can get 0% fail rate in 
Create Monster.  IMO recording the 5 highest scores is enough to keep the 
extinctionists happy.

> 3. 1st, 2nd, 3rd place Fastest Ascension (fewest turns)
> 4. 1st place Fastest for each class

I believe speed to ascension is the best simple way to rank games, so I'd 
like to see the 3 fastest for each class plus the 3 fastest overall.

> 5. 1st, 2nd, 3rd Most Ascensions
> 6. 1st, 2nd, 3rd place Lowest Score Ascensions

Sure.

> 7. Low Score, High Score, Fastest for pacifist conduct

The pacifists already have the lowest scoring category, and that's enough.

> 8. High Score, Fastest for each conduct

High score is meaningless.  If the server is willing and able to track the 
fastest ascension for each conduct, that sounds fine.  

> 9. High Score, Fastest for any conduct combos
> 10. High Score, Fastest Extinctionist (would need patch with birth/death
> info)

Nah.

> 11. Highest weapon enchantment (death -or- ascension)
> 12. Highest armor enchantment (death -or- ascension)
> 13. Most artfacts (death -or- ascension)

Boring!

> 14. Most unique deaths

They already have that.  I dislike it, because it conflicts with any attempt 
to measure the overall skill of the player across all his games, such as 
ascension percentage.  


